<title>POLAND: Polish industrial output down 7.3 pct in November.</title>
<headline>Polish industrial output down 7.3 pct in November.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's industrial output (undajusted) fell 7.3 percent in November after a seven percent rise in October and was 4.5 percent higher than in November 1995, the Central Statistical Office (GUS) said.</p>
<p>Industrial output rose 8.8 percent in the January-November period against the same period last year.</p>
<p> POLISH INDUSTRIAL OUTPUT  NOVEMBER	OCTOBER    NOVEMBER 95</p>
<p> month/month change (pct)	 -7.3	  7.0(7.5)	  0.0</p>
<p> yr/yr change (pct)		  4.5	 13.3(13.9)	 9.7</p>
<p> index (mthly avge 1994=100)    23.4	  na		*39.5</p>
<p> mining m/m change		 -10.8	  8.8(10.3)	16.1</p>
<p> mining yr/yr change		-6.8	 21.4(23.0)	-2.0</p>
<p> manufacturing m/m change	 -8.2	  6.1(6.6)	 -2.7</p>
<p> manufacturing yr/yr change	7.0	 13.3(13.9)	11.7</p>
<p> utilities m/m change		5.3	 13.7(14.0)	16.0</p>
<p> utilities yr/yr change	   -4.7	  5.6(5.9)	  2.8</p>
<p>NOTES - Revised data in brackets. November 1996 and November 1995 had 21 working days while October 1996 had 24 working days. * November 1995 index is based on a monthly average from 1992.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
